The send-back flow proves resolution-scoped rebase review and republishing to the same PR.
Forge integration tests use real git against a local bare repository and the strict gh executable stand-in, including real merge-tree exit-1 conflict evidence and installed-gh offline syntax checks.
The shared RunMergeabilityContract suite runs against both the real boundary and scripted fake, checking exact evidence, repeated reads, ownership of returned path slices, invalid inputs and moved heads.
A notification-failure test proves recovery from the durable observation even when the forge clears before the notification is replayed.
CLI tests exercise command validation, help, actual launch, feedback and replay through the normal advance wiring.
The forge integration and extra refusal/hold/cache tests were added after implementation; they are not claimed as red-first tests.
